1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Your brain is built by two cell lineages that never mix

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:11,658
Two stem-cell populations, separate from gastrulation onward

3
00:00:11,658 --> 00:00:17,487
Otx2 cells build the forebrain and midbrain

4
00:00:17,487 --> 00:00:23,316
Gbx2 cells build the hindbrain

5
00:00:23,316 --> 00:00:29,145
Different chromatin states from the earliest embryonic stages

6
00:00:29,145 --> 00:00:35,703
The same split shows up across species

7
00:00:35,703 --> 00:00:42,261
Lineages that diverged around 550 million years ago

8
00:00:42,261 --> 00:00:48,090
Two lineages, shown in mice. "Two organs" is press framing.
